A refused declaration is shown to the person (ORDER 453). Qt Multimedia's VideoOutput declares a 3D video to the desktop before it attaches anything and, when the desktop refuses, draws the ordinary picture and says why in stereoLayerFailure (qt6-multimedia +stereo3d15). Dragon shows that reason in a message over the video, "This video is shown flat: the desktop refused to show it in 3D (reason).", in the nine languages. Dragon carries no stereo layer of its own: the drawing, the declaration and the failure are Qt Multimedia's, and Dragon keeps its menu, its settings window and its per-file choices.

debian/control: depends on Qt Multimedia +stereo3d15.
